# XCU sccs
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# sccs is a front end to the other SCCS utilities, which are all present or
# all absent together with it (XSI); a missing one makes the test report
# NOTINUSE. Setup uses admin, get and delta directly, never sccs, so a
# fault in sccs cannot spoil it. The SCCS file format is unspecified, so
# nothing reads the files; texts are checked through get, and the layout of
# lists and diagnostics is never compared literally.

assertion  XCU.sccs.001
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With no options sccs prefixes an operand with the SCCS directory and the s. prefix,
           runs the named utility on it, and passes options through, so sccs get -p gives what
           get -p gives on SCCS/s.f: the same text, status and standard error, and no g-file.
note       the description prefixes an operand with the SCCS directory and
           s. only for the plain-name case here; a name with a directory part
           is placed as in the -p example (see assertion 003).
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/001-default-directory.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.002
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -d path makes path the root for the SCCS files: the pathname is prefixed with it,
           whether the path is absolute or relative.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/002-d-option.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.003
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -p path replaces the SCCS directory name, inserted before the last component:
           -p y get a/b reads a/y/s.b, and with -d /x it reads /x/a/y/s.b.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/003-p-option.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.004
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The -d option takes precedence over the PROJECTDIR variable.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/004-d-over-projectdir.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.005
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       PROJECTDIR is the default for -d: a value beginning with a slash is an absolute
           pathname used as the root of the SCCS files.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/005-projectdir-absolute.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.006
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A PROJECTDIR value that does not begin with a slash and names no user with a
           src or source directory is used as a relative pathname for the root.
note       the account-name reading of the value cannot be used; the name
           chosen is one no account is expected to have, so the text's
           "otherwise" applies.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/006-projectdir-relative.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.007
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -r is accepted before the command, which then runs and gives its usual result.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/007-r-option.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.008
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       create makes the SCCS file from the file of the same name, passes admin options
           (-r2 makes the first SID 2.1), and renames the original with a leading comma.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
