assertion  XCU.sccs.009
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       edit is equivalent to get -e: same report, same status, a writable g-file.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/009-edit.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.010
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       info lists the files being edited, and not those that are not.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/010-info.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.011
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      disputed
since      1992
says       info -b is accepted and lists nothing that plain info does not, with an edit of a
           trunk SID and of a branch SID present (the page's parenthesis about branches
           contradicts the usual meaning, so only this is required).
note       disputed: the text says branches are SIDs with two or fewer
           components, which would make trunk SIDs the branches; the usual
           meaning (four components) is the opposite. No reading is chosen:
           the test only requires -b to be accepted and not to list a file that
           plain info omits.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/011-info-b.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.012
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       info -u user lists only files being edited by that user; -U means -u of the
           current user.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/012-info-u.sh

