assertion  XCU.sccs.024
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The syntax guidelines apply to the options before the command: -- ends them,
           so sccs -d root -- get -p f runs get on root's SCCS file.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/024-dashes-sccs.sh

assertion  XCU.sccs.025
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/sccs.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The pseudo-utilities follow the syntax guidelines: -- after the command ends its
           options, so sccs edit -- f works like sccs edit f and sccs info -- succeeds.
nomutant   the SCCS utilities are absent on the machine where this was written, so no fault could be planted and judged; the entry is on ci/pending.list
test       t/025-dashes-pseudo.sh

